<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="688e2f6c-6013-55ba-9832-ea5cea4542ac" activityNameId="61c377ed-9cbf-5f66-8467-abc3b1520d6a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Door, outer, wood-glass, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Door, outer, wood-glass, at plant
The dataset can be applied to describe an average entrance door of a one-family house. The door frame is made of steel (paint coated), the door leaf is made of wood, planked with powder coated aluminium on both sides, with a glass insert (62 % wood, 38% glass). The lock, door handles and frame joints are fabricated from steel. Data are based on a door of 0.8x2.0 m and scaled to 1m2. 1 m2 of the aluminium planked massive wood-glass outer door weighs 36.5 kg. The functional life time for the door frame is 60 years, for the door leaf it is 30 years. Wood input linked to updated supply chain based on information obtained from Frank Werner and input of glazing updated based on QualiBob data. Philippe Stolz, August 2016.\nGeography: Data from producers in Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology represents average European production.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Türen\nUVEK 2022 source file:07152.XML\n\n
UUID: eeed239c-58ca-3bd0-aac2-ab56344428e6
This dataset describes the production of 1m2 (visible area) outer door, (entrance door), including the processes for the installation. Not included are transports from plant to construction site.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The technology represents average European production.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Published study, Internet search 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_eeed239c-58ca-3bd0-aac2-ab56344428e6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
